From: momokind <momokind2002@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hevc: keep the v4l2request hwaccel when only the SPS payload changes

Some streams (HDR Vivid WEB-DL, for instance) repeat their parameter sets
with a new SPS payload but identical format-relevant fields. compare_sps()
compares the raw NAL bytes, so such an SPS becomes a new HEVCSPS object and
hevc_frame_start() calls get_format() again. ff_get_format() uninitializes
the current hwaccel first, which for v4l2request tears down the whole V4L2
session and recreates its buffers. That happens on every repeated parameter
set and causes stalls, dropped packets on buffer allocation failures and,
with frames still queued, a crash in v4l2_request_wait_on_capture().

Keep the hwaccel when the format-relevant SPS fields (pixel format,
dimensions, bit depth) and the single-layer VPS layout are unchanged.
Other hwaccels and real format changes still go through get_format().

--- a/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
@@ -3224,6 +3224,21 @@
     if (l->sps != sps) {
         const HEVCSPS *sps_base = s->layers[0].sps;
         enum AVPixelFormat pix_fmt = sps->pix_fmt;
+        /*
+         * A repeated parameter set can carry a different payload while the
+         * format stays the same (an HDR Vivid SPS VUI that changes per GOP,
+         * for instance). Re-running get_format() would tear the hwaccel
+         * down: for v4l2request that recreates the entire V4L2 session and
+         * all of its buffers for no reason.
+         */
+        const int same_format = l->sps &&
+                                sps->pix_fmt == l->sps->pix_fmt &&
+                                sps->width == l->sps->width &&
+                                sps->height == l->sps->height &&
+                                sps->bit_depth == l->sps->bit_depth &&
+                                sps->vps && l->sps->vps &&
+                                sps->vps->nb_layers < 2 &&
+                                l->sps->vps->nb_layers < 2;
 
         if (l != &s->layers[0]) {
             if (!sps_base) {
@@ -3264,7 +3279,15 @@
         if (l == &s->layers[0]) {
             export_stream_params(s, sps);
 
-            ret = get_format(s, sps);
+            if (same_format && s->avctx->hwaccel &&
+                !strcmp(s->avctx->hwaccel->name, "hevc_v4l2request"))
+            {
+                ret = s->avctx->pix_fmt;
+            }
+            else
+            {
+                ret = get_format(s, sps);
+            }
             if (ret < 0) {
                 set_sps(s, l, NULL);
                 return ret;
